{"claim": "The mind tab (2026-08-16): the agent apps fourth tab - status/statistics/tools/configuration for the autonomous machinery. UI lives in agent.chat control facets, edited ONLY via dev-code-read_control_facet + patch_control_facet (nn_sessionid is a required param; pass empty). The HTTP exec envelope nests the command result under .data ({status,pid,nn_return_type,data}) - unwrap before reading fields; the top-level pid is the EXECUTION id, not a process. Backend: agent-model train_status (train.pid + log tail), get_settings/set_setting (live globals + botd.properties rewrite, secret keys masked/refused), promote_pointer (POST /promote client). Verified in headless Chromium against a disposable running the real server.", "tags": "ui", "confidence": "high", "time": 1786899133189},
{"claim": "The chat pane has a sessions sidebar (2026-08-25): switch between or start conversations without losing the current one, all browser-local.", "detail": "Landed as journaled facet patches p50-p55 on agent.chat. Storage: an index at localStorage key agent.chat.sessions.v1 plus one record per session at agent.chat.s.<id>, each capped at 60 messages / 120 cells (the old single-session cap). Every message persists to its session record as it happens, so switching saves nothing and loads both rendered cells and model context. New sessions are not listed until their first message; the old agent.chat.v1 single-session key auto-migrates into the first sidebar entry on first load. Session titles come from the first user message and shift if early messages age out of the cap. Memory, journals, and the archivist queue are untouched.", "tags": "agent.chat,sessions,sidebar,localStorage,ui,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787660334918},
{"claim": "The chat supports attachments (2026-08-25): 📎 button, drag & drop onto the chat, and paste-screenshot; files save via agent.chat.upload to runtime/agent/uploads/ and the outgoing message gains an [ATTACHED FILES] block of absolute paths, with text files ≤32KB inlined.", "detail": "Landed as journaled patches p56-p59 on agent.chat plus the upload command (hand-rolled base64 decoder, sanitized basename, 20MB client cap). Transport: uploads go as a JSON POST to ../app/exec with sessionid in the querystring, NOT through invokeCommand — that path rides the websocket or GET/JSONP and cannot carry megabytes. Multipart POST was rejected on purpose: app/service/init.rs deletes the per-request temp dir immediately after parsing the parts, before command execution, so tempfile params (write_asset's contract) point at already-deleted files. The model is text-only across every chat_llm arm, so images are not seen as pixels; the agent opens saved paths with its tools.", "tags": "agent.chat,attachments,upload,transport", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787665116676},
{"claim": "The agent chat prepends a hidden context preamble as its own user message ([CONTEXT] + the memory:index fence) ahead of the user's real first question - any consumer that reads 'the first user message' (session titling did) gets the preamble, not the question.", "detail": "Bit the history sidebar: sessTitle() titled every saved session '[CONTEXT] ```memory:index ...'. Fixed 2026-08-25 in agent.chat js (patches p63/p64): title generation skips user messages starting with [CONTEXT], plus a one-time load repair retitling saved sessions from their stored messages. Rule going forward: anything scanning a session's messages for the user's words must skip [CONTEXT]-prefixed user turns.", "tags": "agent.chat,context-injection,session-titles,gotcha,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787681286562},
{"claim": "The plan tab (2026-08-25): a kanban board over kb.plan, in the new agent.plan control mounted as agent.chat's fifth tab via two html patches (the generic tab switcher needed no js/css changes).", "detail": "Backend: agent-plan-board reads kb.plan's memory facet and returns entries plus the facet content hash; agent-plan-move_item swaps the lifecycle token in an entry's tags (preserving other tags/fields) and writes the whole facet through the journaled dev.code.patch_control_facet with the board hash as concurrency token - stale kb.plan answers err stale_base and the UI reloads; agent-plan-add_item files new items via agent.archivist.remember as plan,proposed, confidence medium, author from the calling session. UI: five columns matching the lifecycle tokens epistemic_work derives from (proposed/accepted/in-progress/done/abandoned), drag-to-move, entries lacking a lifecycle token surface in proposed and normalize on first move. Verified live: a roundtrip move landed as kb.plan journal patches. New commands default admin-only.", "tags": "agent.plan,agent.chat,kb.plan,kanban,ui,lifecycle,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787685134242},
{"end": true}]
